      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Salem%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village site was laid out in 1850 and was settled mainly by German immigrants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Salem%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A historic hotel, a doctor's office, an armory, Wagner's General Store, and a gas station with auto parts shop once operated in Lower Salem, though all have closed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Salem%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lower Salem sits on the banks of Duck Creek, north of Marietta and south of Caldwell.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.citydirectory.us/village-lower-salem.html",
